# skhd — app launcher hotkeys.
#
# Single catcher for both keyboards:
#   * Voyager      sends Hyper+N directly from its firmware
#   * Laptop       kanata turns Space-hold + N into Hyper+N
#
# App names still live in one place: .config/karabiner/open-app-slot.sh
# (left in the karabiner directory on purpose, so rolling back to
# Karabiner-Elements needs no file moves).
#
# skhd runs as a normal user agent, so `open -a` works without any
# root/launchctl workaround — which is why kanata does not need the
# `cmd` feature that Homebrew's build omits.

# ---- Ctrl-<key> rewrites, for every keyboard kanata does NOT see ----
#
# kanata is scoped to the built-in keyboard (macos-dev-names-include in
# .config/kanata/kanata.kbd), so its @ctlh / @ctlb / Ctrl-M forks and the
# Ctrl-; defoverride exist ONLY on the laptop. On the Voyager the same chord
# is resolved in QMK firmware and leaves as a literal Ctrl-Opt-H, which macOS
# does not understand -- see below. These lines restore parity by rewriting at
# the event-tap level, which is above the keyboard and therefore keyboard-blind.
#
# Why the chord has to be rewritten at all, rather than composing on its own:
# macOS resolves text commands by ONE exact-chord lookup in AppKit's
# StandardKeyBinding.dict. That table has separate rows for "^h" and for "^?"
# (Delete), both landing on deleteBackward:, and a row for "~^?" (Opt-Delete)
# landing on deleteWordBackward:. There is NO row for "~^h". Ctrl-H is not
# "the Delete key"; it is its own entry, so Option has nothing to modify.
#
# No double-processing on the laptop: kanata rewrites at the HID level, below
# this event tap, so skhd only ever sees the already-converted Opt-Backspace.
#
# skhd matches modifiers EXACTLY, so each combination needs its own line --
# kanata's `unmod` drops Ctrl generically and keeps whatever else is held,
# which is not expressible here. The cross-product is not enumerated; these
# are the combinations that were actually in use.
#
# `backspace` is skhd's name for the Backspace key. `delete` is FORWARD
# delete -- using it here would eat the word AHEAD of the cursor.
#
# Cost: each press forks a short-lived `skhd -k` to synthesize the event.
# Ctrl-H is a high-frequency key, so if it ever feels laggy, that fork is why.
#
# Scope: GUI (Cocoa) apps only, and that is not a bug worth chasing.
#   * Ctrl-Cmd-H cannot work in a terminal -- verified. The legacy key encoding
#     has no bit for Cmd, so the modifier is dropped downstream of skhd. Same
#     reason it fails from the laptop; see .config/wezterm/wezterm.lua.
#   * Ctrl-Opt-H reaches the terminal as ESC DEL, and .zshrc runs `bindkey -v`
#     with KEYTIMEOUT=1, so `^[` is eaten instantly as vi-cmd-mode.
#   Delete-word / delete-line in the terminal are `^W` and `^U`, bound directly
#   in .zshrc. That split is deliberate -- the terminal is its own world.
#
# One asymmetry worth knowing if a chord ever stops working: skhd posts to
# kCGHIDEventTap, which re-merges the modifiers you are PHYSICALLY holding into
# the synthetic event. So the Ctrl you are still holding rides along. Ctrl-Opt-H
# survives because StandardKeyBinding.dict also has a "~^^?" row (Ctrl-Opt-
# Delete) landing on deleteWordBackward:. A chord whose target has only one row
# would break; fixing that needs an in-place event rewrite (Hammerspoon), not
# synthesis.
ctrl - h             : skhd -k "backspace"
ctrl + alt - h       : skhd -k "alt - backspace"
ctrl + cmd - h       : skhd -k "cmd - backspace"
ctrl + shift - h     : skhd -k "shift - backspace"
ctrl - 0x21          : skhd -k "escape"           # Ctrl-[  -> Esc
ctrl - m             : skhd -k "return"           # Ctrl-M  -> Return
ctrl - 0x29          : skhd -k "shift - 0x32"     # Ctrl-;  -> ~

# ---- App launcher ----
cmd + ctrl + alt + shift - 1 : ~/.config/karabiner/open-app-slot.sh 1
cmd + ctrl + alt + shift - 2 : ~/.config/karabiner/open-app-slot.sh 2
cmd + ctrl + alt + shift - 3 : ~/.config/karabiner/open-app-slot.sh 3
cmd + ctrl + alt + shift - 4 : ~/.config/karabiner/open-app-slot.sh 4
cmd + ctrl + alt + shift - 5 : ~/.config/karabiner/open-app-slot.sh 5
cmd + ctrl + alt + shift - 6 : ~/.config/karabiner/open-app-slot.sh 6
cmd + ctrl + alt + shift - 7 : ~/.config/karabiner/open-app-slot.sh 7
